## Intentionally excluded and known gaps

- `crosshair_grenadelauncher_ammunition.muigraph` does not contain the same
  `DamageDealt` ordinary/fatal gates and requires separate research.
- `hud_combat_damage_direction.muigraph` controls incoming-damage direction,
  not outgoing weapon hit markers, so this build does not replace it.
- The following additional variants are known to exist but were not available
  in the current extracted vanilla corpus and are not covered yet:
  - `crosshair_burst_assault_rifle_rokana_raider_charge_ammunition.muigraph`
  - `crosshair_pistol_ion_shock_overheat.muigraph`

Please report any other weapon that still displays hit or fatal markers.

## Test status

Verified in game:

- First two tiers of all three Kay blaster slots, including charge behavior
- E-11, with normal crosshair and ammunition UI
- DLT-A20 Sniper, both scoped in and scoped out
- Combined-build startup, loading, and regression checks

The DLT-A20's exact graph assignment has not been isolated, so its result is
recorded as functional batch coverage rather than a confirmed filename map.

Not directly verified yet:

- Third-tier Kay configurations
- Most individual pickup-weapon variants
- Known gaps listed above

## Compatibility

This mod conflicts at the file level with anything that replaces one of the
16 included `.muigraph` files. Whichever mod wins the loose-file conflict will
determine the result.

Do not combine it with the original zero-file Disable Hitmarkers package. The
original package will remove the same UI graphs entirely if it wins the
conflict.

## Validation

Every included graph is guarded by its exact filename and vanilla SHA-256.
The build process then verifies that:

- Each `DamageDealt`, `Has Dealt Damage`, `Fatal`, and constant-false target is
  structurally unique.
- Only the intended setter records change.
- All `DamageDealt` output records remain byte-identical.
- Strings, descriptors, pool counts, graph layouts, and file sizes remain
  unchanged.
- Every emitted graph reparses successfully.
- The complete research tool currently passes 34 automated tests.

Across the 16 files, 34 compiled setter records are redirected. Fifteen files
contain one ordinary/fatal pair; the charge-up marksman rifle contains two.

## Reporting problems or missing coverage

Please include as much of the following as possible:

```text
Game version/build:
Mod loader and version:
Other crosshair/UI mods:
Weapon name:
Weapon configuration or upgrade tier:
Scoped or unscoped:
What remained visible or stopped working:
Did the issue persist after reloading the save:
Crash timing, if applicable:
```

A screenshot or short clip is helpful for remaining markers or broken UI, but
the weapon name and configuration are the most important details.

